The area of quadrilateral \(DBEF\) is \(8\).

The coordinates are \(D(0,3)\), \(B(0,0)\), \(E(4,0)\), and \(F\left(\frac{8}{3},2\right)\). Using the shoelace formula with vertices in order \(D \to B \to E \to F \to D\):

\[
\begin{aligned}
\text{Area} &= \frac{1}{2}\left| (0\cdot0 + 0\cdot0 + 4\cdot2 + \frac{8}{3}\cdot3) - (3\cdot0 + 0\cdot4 + 0\cdot\frac{8}{3} + 2\cdot0) \right| \\
&= \frac{1}{2}\left| (0+0+8+8) - (0+0+0+0) \right| = \frac{1}{2} \cdot 16 = 8.
\end{aligned}
\]

Alternatively, splitting the quadrilateral along diagonal \(BF\) gives triangles \(BDF\) and \(BEF\) with areas \(4\) and \(4\), summing to \(8\).

